# The client is one page at `/`, so every path that is not a real file has to serve it.
#
# `/n/<petname>/` is the route that opens a machine's panel in an iframe. The service worker
# answers it before the network is ever consulted — but on the very first load, before the worker
# is installed, that URL goes to the host, and a 404 there puts the browser into a dead frame on
# exactly the request that matters. Serving the page is correct: the worker takes over from there.
#
# `200` is a rewrite, not a redirect: the URL the client sees stays `/n/<petname>/`, which is what
# the worker keys on to know which node it is answering for.
/*    /index.html    200
